{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the only protected observation is the top-level data variable `y`, which is scored once by the built-in `multi_normal_cholesky` distribution. The original model computed parameter-dependent covariance matrices before the parameter priors, which violates SafeStan's parameter-use ordering rule. The safe version declares those local matrices first, places the existing built-in priors for `rho`, `alpha`, and `sigma` before any parameter-dependent computation, then computes the covariance and scores `y`. This is a mechanical reordering that preserves the posterior/log density. No data fields were added or changed; `data_safe.json` equals the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  vector gp_pred_rng(array[] real x2,
                     vector y1, array[] real x1,
                     real alpha, real rho, real sigma, real delta) {
    int N1 = rows(y1);
    int N2 = size(x2);
    vector[N2] f2;
    {
      matrix[N1, N1] K =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x1, alpha, rho)
                         + diag_matrix(rep_vector(square(sigma), N1));
      matrix[N1, N1] L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);

      vector[N1] L_K_div_y1 = mdivide_left_tri_low(L_K, y1);
      vector[N1] K_div_y1 = mdivide_right_tri_low(L_K_div_y1', L_K)';
      matrix[N1, N2] k_x1_x2 = gp_exp_quad_cov(x1, x2, alpha, rho);
      vector[N2] f2_mu = (k_x1_x2' * K_div_y1);
      matrix[N1, N2] v_pred = mdivide_left_tri_low(L_K, k_x1_x2);
      matrix[N2, N2] cov_f2 =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x2, alpha, rho) - v_pred' * v_pred
                              + diag_matrix(rep_vector(delta, N2));
      f2 = multi_normal_rng(f2_mu, cov_f2);
    }
    return f2;
  }
}

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
  vector[N] y;

  int<lower=1> N_predict;
  array[N_predict] real x_predict;
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  matrix[N, N] cov;
  matrix[N, N] L_cov;

  // P[rho < 2.0] = 0.01
  // P[rho > 10] = 0.01
  rho ~ inv_gamma(8.91924, 34.5805);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  cov =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho)
        + diag_matrix(rep_vector(square(sigma), N));
  L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);

  y ~ multi_normal_cholesky(rep_vector(0, N), L_cov);
}

generated quantities {
  vector[N_predict] f_predict = gp_pred_rng(x_predict, y, x, alpha, rho, sigma, 1e-10);
  vector[N_predict] y_predict;
  for (n in 1:N_predict)
    y_predict[n] = normal_rng(f_predict[n], sigma);
}
